WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.568
Now, Hunter Biden said

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.103
that his father didn't do anything wrong

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:05.338
and that Joe Biden never benefited

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:07.007
financially from his business dealings.

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:08.708
And here's the truth.

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:09.509
Legal scholars

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:11.611
and even Republicans have agreed to this.

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:12.112
They have agreed

00:00:12.112 --> 00:00:13.179
that there has been no evidence

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:17.517
put forth of wrongdoing by the president.

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:20.153
The facts haven't taken me to that point

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:21.421
where I can say

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:23.623
that the president is guilty of anything.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:24.090
I don't know that

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:24.824
you gonna see a high crime

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:25.392
or misdemeanor.

00:00:25.392 --> 00:00:27.227
We don't have the evidence now,

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:29.729
but we may find it later.

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:32.499
So they say that they have no evidence,

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:34.601
and yet every single Republican

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.202
in the House of Representatives,

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:39.706
221 people, every single Republican,

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:41.674
221 people

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.143
without evidence voted to launch

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:43.676
an impeachment

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:44.844
inquiry, an inquiry

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:46.079
that is designed to distract

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:47.514
from the mounting evidence in the case

00:00:47.514 --> 00:00:48.548
involving Trump's efforts

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:50.550
to overturn the 2020 election.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.484
In fact, tonight,

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:53.219
we have exclusive new audio

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.421
of a December 2020

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:55.922
Oval Office meeting with then

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:57.057
President Trump.

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:57.757
pro-Trump attorney

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:58.892
Kenneth Cesaro

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.894
is telling Michigan prosecutors

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:02.028
that at the meeting

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:04.531
he told Trump how he could still win

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:07.233
using so-called alternate electors.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:10.236
Listen to this part.

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:12.839
So I ended up explaining

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:14.674
that Arizona was still

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:15.809
hypothetically possible

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:18.144
because the also electors had voted.

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:19.546
And I explained the whole logic

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:21.281
because the also electors had voted.

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:24.284
We had more time with the allegation.

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:25.885
Of course, Trump embraced

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.120
Cesaro's theory,

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.588
continuing to falsely claim

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:30.790
that he won the election,

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.592
even though now we know person

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:33.860
after person of experts

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:34.994
sat the Oval Office

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:36.029
and told him that he'd lost

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:37.530
and that he accepted that.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.265
Cesaro, of course, is an unindicted

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:40.400
coconspirator in Trump's

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.634
federal case as well.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:42.469
We're going to get to much more

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:43.770
of that exclusive audio in a moment.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:44.204
But first,

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:45.805
I want to get to Manu Raju on Capitol

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:47.307
Hill on the impeachment vote

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:48.575
that just passed.

00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:49.943
Manu, that vote just happened,

00:01:49.943 --> 00:01:51.211
as I emphasized.

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:54.114
Every single Republican supported it.

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:55.648
You've been talking to some of them.

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:57.283
What are they telling you?

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.418
Yeah, a lot of them supported it

00:01:58.418 --> 00:01:59.052
because they said

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:00.920
the investigation should continue.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.422
But I pressed a number of them

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:03.723
about whether they believe

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:04.791
that President Biden

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:06.326
should actually be impeached.

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:07.360
He would just be the fourth

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.895
president in American history

00:02:08.895 --> 00:02:10.630
to be charged with high crimes

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:11.498
and misdemeanors.

00:02:11.498 --> 00:02:13.900
An incredibly high bar to me.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:14.901
And a lot of those members

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:17.403
I talked to are saying they have not yet

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:19.472
met that bar in fact, that, frankly,

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.241
they say that the impeachment inquiry

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:22.742
needs to gather the evidence

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:23.443
that they're searching

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:24.410
for, tying

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.879
Joe Biden, accusing Joe

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:27.847
Biden of taking direct action

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:30.283
to benefit his son's businesses

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:31.551
while the president

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:33.153
for the president was in office

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:34.287
as vice president.

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:35.889
They don't have that drug link yet.

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:37.724
But a lot of these members are hoping

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:39.259
that they can find that evidence

00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:40.727
so they could support impeachment,

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:42.295
the impeachment, ultimately.

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:43.263
Now, some of those members

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:44.664
come from swing districts

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:46.065
and they are indicating to me,

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:47.333
yes, they'll vote now

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:48.701
to move forward on this inquiry.

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:50.503
But whether they vote to impeach him

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:54.641
is another question.

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:55.041
All right.

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:56.176
You ready to go as

00:02:56.176 --> 00:02:57.410
far as impeaching the president?

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:58.578
No, I'm going to let the committees

00:02:58.578 --> 00:02:59.879
continue their work,

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:01.314
develop their articles.

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:02.815
If they develop articles of impeachment,

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:04.584
show the show their evidence,

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:05.818
and then we'll make a separate choice

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:06.052
there.

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:07.887
How close are you to being ready

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:09.022
to support

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.190
impeachment, actual

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:11.858
impeachment of the president?

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:13.126
We're not there.

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:15.061
We we voted tonight

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:17.730
to allow for the investigation

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:18.831
to continue.

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:22.268
This was a vote to authorize

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:24.837
the investigation formally

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:25.772
because the White House

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:26.773
has taken the position

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:28.808
that it was an informal inquiry

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:32.045
and they didn't need to comply.

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:34.214
And this is going to put Speaker Johnson

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:36.749
in a bind in the weeks ahead

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:39.319
because a number of members on his right

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:41.187
are pushing for impeachment

00:03:41.187 --> 00:03:43.022
of the president of the United States.

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:43.890
But some of those swing

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.225
district members that you heard

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:46.025
there are still

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:47.460
waiting for this investigation

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:48.161
to gather

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:50.530
even more information to prove

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.632
that Joe Biden acted corruptly.

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:54.200
Then they said they can charge him

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.868
with those high crimes and misdemeanors.

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:56.436
So, Aaron,

00:03:56.436 --> 00:03:58.171
you can see the bind, given that

00:03:58.171 --> 00:03:58.972
Mike Johnson

00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:00.840
can only afford to lose three

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:01.808
Republican votes

00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:03.376
on any straight party line vote,

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:04.544
whether he can get there

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:05.878
remains a huge question.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:06.412
All right, Manu,

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:08.114
thank you very much on Capitol Hill.

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:09.549
Of course, speaking to those congressmen.

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:10.450
And I want to go now

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:11.517
to the Democratic Congressman

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:13.019
Ro Khanna of California.

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:14.120
He's on the committee that Hunter

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.388
Biden, Biden, defiantly

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:16.923
refuse to appear before today. Right.

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:18.691
Saying that he wanted to testify

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:19.892
publicly in front of in

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:20.860
front of everyone.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:21.427
So, Congressman,

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:23.596
the impeachment inquiry is now

00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:25.231
a done deal out of the committee.

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:26.232
Are you prepared

00:04:26.232 --> 00:04:27.600
for televised

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.402
impeachment hearings, accusations

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:30.336
and everything else

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:32.071
that this investigation

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:36.042
will likely entail in an election year?

00:04:36.109 --> 00:04:37.577
Urn, it's very sad because

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:39.545
the American people want us focused

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:41.381
on the cost of living.

00:04:41.381 --> 00:04:42.548
The housing affordability

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:44.250
crisis is a total distraction.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:46.219
I think actually is going to backfire

00:04:46.219 --> 00:04:47.620
on the Republicans.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:48.488
You saw

00:04:48.488 --> 00:04:50.323
impeachment hearings in the past

00:04:50.323 --> 00:04:52.158
have actually benefited

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:53.860
the person, the president.

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:55.194
And I think this is

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:56.529
not just a waste of time.

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:58.865
It's politically damaging for them.

00:04:58.865 --> 00:05:00.800
So your colleague, Ken Buck,

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.068
the one Republican

00:05:02.068 --> 00:05:03.503
who had expressed hesitation

00:05:03.503 --> 00:05:04.570
about voting for the impeachment,

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:05.471
he was hesitant,

00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:06.906
but he ultimately did vote for it,

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:08.107
as he said they all did.

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:09.175
When I spoke with him

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:11.110
on Monday, Congressman,

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:13.313
he criticized the White House

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:14.514
for saying

00:05:14.514 --> 00:05:16.716
that it would not hand over records

00:05:16.716 --> 00:05:17.950
unless they were forced to do

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:19.585
so by an impeachment proceeding. Right.

00:05:19.585 --> 00:05:20.887
This whole point that, well,

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:22.021
this is informal,

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:22.989
We haven't been subpoenaed.

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:23.589
We're not going to hand

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:24.590
over the documents.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:25.458
So Hunter Biden

00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:27.060
today, then congressman, referenced

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:27.860
financial records

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.462
in his defiant press conference

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:30.363
very specifically.

00:05:30.363 --> 00:05:31.064
And I wanted to play

00:05:31.064 --> 00:05:34.901
one thing that he said.

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:37.070
James Colmer,

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:38.971
Jim Jordan,

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:42.175
Jason Smith and their colleagues

00:05:42.241 --> 00:05:44.844
have distorted the facts

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:46.112
by cherry picking lines

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:48.014
from a bank statement,

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:49.182
manipulating texts.

00:05:49.182 --> 00:05:50.350
I sent

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:52.518
editing the testimony of my friends

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:55.088
and former business partners

00:05:55.088 --> 00:05:56.823
and misstating personal information

00:05:56.823 --> 00:05:59.425
that was stolen from me.

00:05:59.425 --> 00:05:59.926
Now, Congressman,

00:05:59.926 --> 00:06:01.260
kind of all of this is true

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.929
as Hunter Biden lays it out.

00:06:02.929 --> 00:06:04.464
Why won't the White House and Hunter

00:06:04.464 --> 00:06:06.566
Biden just hand over the records?

00:06:06.566 --> 00:06:07.133
Because, you know,

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:08.534
so they can't just cherry pick. Right.

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:09.602
Put them all out there.

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:11.671
If that would absolve themselves

00:06:11.671 --> 00:06:13.840
of these accusations,

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:16.676
because there's no evidence or allegation

00:06:16.676 --> 00:06:18.745
that the president has done anything

00:06:18.745 --> 00:06:20.346
even slightly wrong in his role

00:06:20.346 --> 00:06:21.180
as president.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.115
This has been litigated

00:06:22.115 --> 00:06:23.483
for five years and it's

00:06:23.483 --> 00:06:25.485
rich for the Republicans

00:06:25.485 --> 00:06:27.286
to be demanding all this release

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:29.222
of personal financial information

00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:30.256
when they're leading candidate

00:06:30.256 --> 00:06:31.023
Donald Trump doesn't

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:32.458
even release his taxes.

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:33.893
Joe Biden has provided

00:06:33.893 --> 00:06:36.062
far more financial information

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:37.263
than anything Biden has.

00:06:37.263 --> 00:06:38.698
This is a witch hunt.

00:06:38.698 --> 00:06:40.233
And here's what I haven't heard.

00:06:40.233 --> 00:06:41.567
I haven't heard the Republicans

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:43.770
say what has President Biden

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:45.805
since he's been president done wrong?

00:06:45.805 --> 00:06:47.707
That's why you impeach someone.

00:06:47.707 --> 00:06:49.375
So Chairman Jordan

00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:50.042
on the committee write,

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:51.144
your chairman, Jim Jordan,

00:06:51.144 --> 00:06:52.178
focused on something Hunter

00:06:52.178 --> 00:06:54.781
Biden said at his press conference,

00:06:54.781 --> 00:06:55.715
which is that his father

00:06:55.715 --> 00:06:57.450
wasn't, quote, financially involved in

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:58.251
Hunter's business.

00:06:58.251 --> 00:06:59.886
I just played that part of what he said

00:06:59.886 --> 00:07:00.586
a few moments ago,

00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:02.388
but he said he wasn't financially,

00:07:02.388 --> 00:07:03.089
that there was no

00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:04.724
he was not financially involved.

00:07:04.724 --> 00:07:06.025
And Jordan says that

00:07:06.025 --> 00:07:07.560
that's significant, that this shows

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:08.561
the story is shifting.

00:07:08.561 --> 00:07:09.729
He says first,

00:07:09.729 --> 00:07:11.030
President Biden had no involvement

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:12.031
at all in Hunter's business.

00:07:12.031 --> 00:07:14.033
Now it's just no financial involvement

00:07:14.033 --> 00:07:17.403
in Hunter's business. Do you

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:19.472
support the chairman's

00:07:19.472 --> 00:07:20.306
focus on now

00:07:20.306 --> 00:07:23.309
the use of the adjective financially?

00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:24.610
I just don't understand

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:25.378
what all this is about.

00:07:25.378 --> 00:07:26.479
If they want to make this case

00:07:26.479 --> 00:07:27.980
in a campaign, fine.

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:28.848
Everything President

00:07:28.848 --> 00:07:30.450
Biden has done since kindergarten

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:32.185
can be litigated in a campaign.

00:07:32.185 --> 00:07:33.119
And they've been doing this

00:07:33.119 --> 00:07:34.187
for the past five years.

00:07:34.187 --> 00:07:36.322
But you can't impeach a sitting

00:07:36.322 --> 00:07:37.990
president of the United States

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:40.793
for conduct That was years ago.

00:07:40.793 --> 00:07:41.894
First of all, there's no evidence

00:07:41.894 --> 00:07:42.962
that he did anything wrong.

00:07:42.962 --> 00:07:43.429
But it's

00:07:43.429 --> 00:07:43.896
they're going

00:07:43.896 --> 00:07:44.997
after things that he did

00:07:44.997 --> 00:07:47.300
potentially as vice president.

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:48.267
I mean,

00:07:48.267 --> 00:07:49.068
can you imagine

00:07:49.068 --> 00:07:50.136
if the Democrats had said,

00:07:50.136 --> 00:07:51.437
we're going to impeach Donald Trump

00:07:51.437 --> 00:07:52.772
for all the bad things he did

00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:54.073
before he became president?

00:07:54.073 --> 00:07:55.508
We focused on action

00:07:55.508 --> 00:07:56.476
while he was president,

00:07:56.476 --> 00:07:59.479
and they have not even had an allegation

00:07:59.545 --> 00:08:00.546
that this president has done

00:08:00.546 --> 00:08:02.515
anything wrong since he's been in office.

00:08:02.515 --> 00:08:02.882
All right.

00:08:02.882 --> 00:08:03.483
Congressman Cohen,

00:08:03.483 --> 00:08:04.784
I appreciate your time. Thank you.

